                    },
                    "message": "Updated."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Host is broader term and what I see in the backend at like \nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/d886ce89fe66c128b3ab492e530ad48fa0c1b4eb/architecture/code-update/host-code-update.md?plain=1#L1\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fdocs%20host&type=code"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I added some folks to this review"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, always fun with these types of terms.  \nFor this instance:  \"Bios\" used instead of \"Host\" when dealing with data from /redfish/v1/Systems/{SystemId}/Bios\nand resources with a \"bios\" odata.id"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Adriana Kobylak",
                        "email": "anoo@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "anoo1"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this change is ok since it's trying to follow the Redfish schema naming.\nAnd seems throughout the code, these term have been interchangeable in general.\n\nThe code update repo refers to the host/bios update option as 'host-bios-upgrade' (https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/blob/master/meson.options#L12).\n\nAnd even though the README in the OpenPower update repo (https://github.com/openbmc/openpower-pnor-code-mgmt) refers to 'host', there are multiple script files in that repo with 'bios' in their name.\n\nThe only term that seems to use 'host' only is 'hostfw' (https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fopenbmc+hostfw&type=code&p=1) but that is currently more of a build environment configuration, although PLDM also uses it this term, but it's understood that PLDM is a communication protocol to the host."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "I am going to let this in unless anyone objects (will give a few days)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
